## ⚠️ Problems Without Version Control

Relying on manual tools or change sets without a Version Control System (VCS) like Git places an enterprise org in a constant state of technical risk:

* **Zero Historical Audit Trail:** Without a VCS, there is no master ledger showing who changed a validation rule, when an Apex trigger was altered, or why a field permission was dropped. Tracking down the root cause of a production outage becomes an exercise in guesswork.
* **Environment Drift:** Sandboxes quickly drift away from production configuration baselines. Developers end up testing logic in environments that do not mirror reality, resulting in features passing locally but failing completely upon production deployment.
* **The "Silent Overwrite":** Multiple developers working out of a shared sandbox routinely save over each other's logic. Whoever clicks "Save" last wins, wiping out hours of peer development without triggering any platform warning flags.

